  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a twenty-four-song set at the 9:30 Club in Washington, DC, on Tuesday, November 7, 2017 [1]. This concert was the second night of a two-day engagement, following a previous show at the same venue on November 6, 2017 [3]. The recording, captured from the front and center with a zoom lens in the shirt pocket, spans one hundred minutes [1]. The setlist draws from various albums, including “Goths,” “We Shall All Be Healed,” and “Heretic Pride” [1]. Notable tracks include “Sun Song,” which was a bustout first appearing in 221 archived shows, and “Beautiful Gas Mask,” which is rare with only eight archived performances [1]. The band also played “Stench of the Unburied” as a rare encore [1]. The uploader described the night as amazing and encouraged listeners to purchase merchandise as a thank you [1]. A single listener rated the recording five out of five stars [1]. A review by Ary Hartman of this specific recording expressed delight at hearing the recorder’s spoken comments, noting that such banter makes listening to concert recordings fun [2]. The set included spoken introductions and stories about the song “Shelved” [1]. This performance is the 241st of 467 in the archive’s collection for the performer [3]. The show was promoted by a poster credited to parklifedc.com [4].",
